{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310660,"nonce":"YdkW6iBeHDQN7McJyj1vMZ12/VU=","title":"FIXED 313c89d9: a store to a Null\u003cInt\u003e class field landed at BYTE offset index (gep *u8 scaled by 1 in every tier) and trampled the header ...","message":"**THE BUG (f33f438, fixed 313c89d9, 2026-09-18):** a boxed `Null\u003cT\u003e` field's\nIrType is `Ptr(U8)`, and every tier's GEP rule scaled `Ptr(U8|I8)` by ONE\nBYTE. `n = 7` on field index 3 wrote 8 bytes at byte 3: header's top byte\nand field 1's low 3 bytes gone. Loads agreed with stores so `n` read back\nfine while `kid.v` read 1024 and `Reflect.field(this,\"kid\")` crashed on a\ntruncated pointer. Fix: only `*i8` is byte-addressed (LLVM, Cranelift,\ninterpreter, C, WASM) — every byte-buffer emitter spells it `Ptr(I8)`.\n\n**FOUND ON THE WAY, same commit:**\n- ctor field-init lowering (`expr/functions.rs`) stored initializers RAW:\n  `n:Null\u003cInt\u003e = 44` put 44 in a slot every reader unboxes (fault=0x2c).\n  It boxes via `maybe_box_value` now.\n- class-field RTTI `ParamType` had no Array/anon kind: `Reflect.field` /\n  `d.xs` handed an Array field back as an INT BOX holding the pointer.\n  `IrField.shape` (Class/Array/Anonymous) → `ParamType::Array/Anon/Object`.\n- call boundary now unboxes String/Array/anon formals by tag\n  (`haxe_unbox_if_tag`), not only scalars (74b3bef, Issue9217's crash).\n\n**HOW IT WAS FOUND:** a runtime trace dumping the object's 4 slots\n(`slots=[\"0xdd48f4\",\"0x71c000000\",...]`) — the corruption PATTERN (top byte\nof slot 0 + low 3 bytes of slot 1 zeroed) named the mechanism: an 8-byte\nstore at byte offset 3 = field index 3. Read the slot dump before theorising.\n\n**TRAP THAT COST AN HOUR:** compared against a HEAD binary COPIED to /tmp —\nsee [[feedback_conformance_must_use_in_repo_binary]]. Also: the debug\n`eprintln` build \"fixed\" a crash — layout-sensitive UB moves; that is a\nsignal, not a fix.\n\nFixture: haxe-conformance/regressions/NullableFieldSlots.hx. Conformance\n536 -\u003e 536 (no row depended on it; the corpus barely writes Null\u003cInt\u003e\nfields), suite 207/0/1, fixtures 19/19.\n\n**FOLLOW-UP LANDED 56bee624 (issue b316acb):** every item above fixed, plus\n`Sys.println(non-String)` (printed nothing / passed the raw value — it now\nstringifies like Std.string), enums by RTTI (`haxe_enum_to_string[_boxed]`,\nString params unquoted as Haxe prints them), a class instance held as\nDynamic reaches its own `toString` via `haxe_type_register_to_string` from\n`__vtable_init__` (fn_ref = closure record `[code, env]`: DEREF it), else\nprints the class name. Rule added: a resolved stdlib static call DECLARED\nto return Dynamic yields a box (`note_dynamic_stdlib_result`) — and a\nbinding typed as a STRUCTURE from a Dynamic still reads BY NAME\n(`raw_anon_symbols`), because the unboxed handle's shape is unknown\n(Json.parse → typedef: by-index read gave 0 and lost Issue9590 for a run).\n**df29e56 FIXED cc70fe31:** the stdlib merge (compilation/driver.rs) replaces\nfunctions BY BARE NAME and a stdlib IMPORT's methods are deliberately\nunprotected (\"placeholder bodies\") — so a body-less `copy` extern in the\nruntime-wrapper module replaced `haxe.Int64.copy` and every caller trapped\n(\"can't resolve symbol copy\" at Cranelift finalize, or a compiler panic =\nTestDefaultArgs' COMPILE_FAIL). Rule now: a body-less stdlib stub never\nreplaces a function that has a body. Any stdlib method sharing a bare name\nwith a wrapper stub was exposed to this. Stdlib toStrings register too now.\nTRAPS: (1) a `fn_ref` value is a closure record `[code, env]` and its code\nspeaks the CLOSURE ABI `(env, args..)` — call it that way from the runtime\n(the ctor wrappers already did; my `f(obj)` \"worked\" on WithTs only because\nits body never read `this`). (2) only the module that LOWERED a method may\nregister it (`function_map`): the user module's merged import copy of\nStringBuf.toString faulted at entry.\nStill wrong: `var y:Null\u003cFloat\u003e = obj.missing` from a parsed object is not\nnull; an erased generic returning Float prints its bits through concat;\n`Std.string(map)` prints the class name (runtime-backed, no Haxe toString).\n\n- Index summary moved from MEMORY.md (2026-10-18): FIXED 313c89d9/56bee624/cc70fe31 (536-\u003e537): `Null\u003cInt\u003e` FIELD STORE at a BYTE offset (`gep *u8` scaled by 1); Std.string/concat/println unified (enums by RTTI, class toString via fn_ref registry — a fn_ref's code speaks the CLOSURE ABI `(env, this)`); the stdlib merge replaced `Int64.copy` with a body-less `copy` stub BY BARE NAME. A Dynamic-returning stdlib call is a box; a STRUCTURE typed from a Dynamic reads BY NAME.\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `bugs_null_field_slot_byte_gep` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}